  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xE9;ponse d&#x2019;urgence pour la protection des moyens d&#x2019;existence des m&#xE9;nages vuln&#xE9;rables affect&#xE9;s par l&#x2019;ins&#xE9;curit&#xE9; et les d&#xE9;placements de population (Centre Nord, Est et Nord du Burkina Faso).</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide food security assistance to vulnerable communities affected by conflict-related displacement in Ouahigouya, Boulsa, Kongoussi, and Bogande. This FAO project aims to preserve the livelihoods of vulnerable people in areas with high security challenges by improving and diversifying their diet and sources of income by providing gardening inputs and animal feed. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 23,800 people, including 9,892 women, 3,193 men, 10,715 children, and 246 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
